## Design notes (context, not instructions to change anything)
- `src/index.css` declares exactly one token — `--font-sans: 'Plus Jakarta Sans'`. There is no colour palette in the theme block; every colour in this project is a Tailwind arbitrary value written inline (`bg-[#050507]`, `bg-[#101116]`, `bg-[#181920]`). That is deliberate, and it is why there is no `tailwind.config.js` to look for.
- The background video carries **no overlay of any kind** — no scrim, no gradient, no `bg-black/40`. The comment in `App.tsx` says so explicitly. The headline is readable because the footage is already dark on the left. Adding a scrim to "fix" contrast is the one change that would visibly break this design.
- All four modals are a single conditional block in `App.tsx` keyed off one `modalOpen` state of a union type, not four components. Keep them inline; splitting them into files changes nothing visually but is not what the source does.
- `showToast` clears itself with a 3200ms timeout and guards the clear with `curr === message`, so a second toast fired inside the window is not cancelled by the first one's timer. Keep that guard.
- The avatar row in the hero and the dashboard user photo are hotlinked Unsplash URLs with sizing parameters baked into the query string. They are left as-is deliberately. Do not swap them for local files, and do not strip the `w`/`h`/`q` parameters.
- `SubtleTextRipple` is imported by `HeroContent`, not by `App.tsx`. It wraps the headline and is the only motion in the project that is not a plain CSS transition.
